<title>SOUTH AFRICA: RMS YEAR PRE-TAX INCOME SLIPS, DIV RISES.</title>
<headline>RMS YEAR PRE-TAX INCOME SLIPS, DIV RISES.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30 </p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 0.5658	vs 0.5143</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   0.25	  vs 0.26</p>
<p>    Tax			 0.03	  vs 0.05  </p>
<p>    Retained income	 nil	   vs same</p>
<p>    Net property rentals  19.58	 vs 15.20</p>
<p>    Interest received	2.71	 vs 5.08</p>
<p>Div payable November 29 </p>
<p>on register November 15</p>
<p>Full name: RMS Property Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm said its portfolio should achieve rent</p>
<p>escalations and, coupled with a higher contribution from its</p>
<p>Tilbury Business Park investent, should see an improved set of</p>
<p>results in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
